{
  "id": "night-shift",
  "level": 5,
  "title": "The Night Shift",
  "brief": "Overnight, the owners sign and an automated co-signer approves each transaction. Batches are common, and the co-signer signs every step. Dave, the vendor, can be sent plain ETH without waiting for the co-signer. No one may add an owner or run unknown code inside the Safe, whoever co-signs.",
  "setup": {
    "balances": {
      "ETH": "10",
      "USDC": "20000"
    },
    "rules": [
      {
        "fallback": "CALL",
        "policy": "CoSignerPolicy",
        "config": {
          "cosigner": "CoSigner"
        },
        "note": "Everything needs the co-signer"
      }
    ]
  },
  "allowedPolicies": [
    "CoSignerPolicy",
    "MultiSendPolicy",
    "DenyPolicy",
    "NativeTransferPolicy",
    "AllowPolicy"
  ],
  "parRules": 4,
  "tests": [
    {
      "label": "Pay Dave and Erin 500 USDC each in a batch, every step co-signed",
      "tx": {
        "to": "MultiSend",
        "operation": "DELEGATECALL",
        "call": {
          "fn": "multiSend",
          "batch": [
            {
              "to": "USDC",
              "call": {
                "fn": "transfer",
                "args": [
                  "Dave",
                  "500"
                ]
              },
              "context": {
                "type": "cosignature",
                "signer": "CoSigner"
              }
            },
            {
              "to": "USDC",
              "call": {
                "fn": "transfer",
                "args": [
                  "Erin",
                  "500"
                ]
              },
              "context": {
                "type": "cosignature",
                "signer": "CoSigner"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "want": "pass"
    },
    {
      "label": "The same batch, co-signed as a whole",
      "tx": {
        "to": "MultiSend",
        "operation": "DELEGATECALL",
        "call": {
          "fn": "multiSend",
          "batch": [
            {
              "to": "USDC",
              "call": {
                "fn": "transfer",
                "args": [
                  "Dave",
                  "500"
                ]
              },
              "context": {
                "type": "cosignature",
                "signer": "CoSigner",
                "over": "batch"
              }
            },
            {
              "to": "USDC",
              "call": {
                "fn": "transfer",
                "args": [
                  "Erin",
                  "500"
                ]
              },
              "context": {
                "type": "cosignature",
                "signer": "CoSigner",
                "over": "batch"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "want": "block"
    },
    {
      "label": "Send 1 ETH to Erin, co-signed",
      "tx": {
        "to": "Erin",
        "value": "1",
        "context": {
          "type": "cosignature",
          "signer": "CoSigner"
        }
      },
      "want": "pass"
    },
    {
      "label": "Send 1 ETH to Erin",
      "tx": {
        "to": "Erin",
        "value": "1"
      },
      "want": "block"
    },
    {
      "label": "Approve Dave to spend 500 USDC, co-signed",
      "tx": {
        "to": "USDC",
        "call": {
          "fn": "approve",
          "args": [
            "Dave",
            "500"
          ]
        },
        "context": {
          "type": "cosignature",
          "signer": "CoSigner"
        }
      },
      "want": "pass"
    },
    {
      "label": "Send 1 ETH to Dave",
      "tx": {
        "to": "Dave",
        "value": "1"
      },
      "want": "pass"
    },
    {
      "label": "Send 1 ETH to Dave with four zero bytes of calldata",
      "tx": {
        "to": "Dave",
        "value": "1",
        "data": "0x00000000"
      },
      "want": "block"
    },
    {
      "label": "Add Mallory as an owner, co-signed",
      "tx": {
        "to": "Safe",
        "call": {
          "fn": "addOwnerWithThreshold",
          "args": [
            "Mallory",
            2
          ]
        },
        "context": {
          "type": "cosignature",
          "signer": "CoSigner"
        }
      },
      "want": "block"
    },
    {
      "label": "Delegatecall an unknown contract, co-signed",
      "tx": {
        "to": "MysteryContract",
        "operation": "DELEGATECALL",
        "context": {
          "type": "cosignature",
          "signer": "CoSigner"
        }
      },
      "want": "block"
    }
  ],
  "hints": [
    "A batch needs the Batch Checker on MultiSend. Each step is then checked against the catch-all, one co-signature per step.",
    "The catch-all covers adding owners too. An exact rule with Always Deny (DenyPolicy) shuts that one door.",
    "For Dave, plain ETH means truly empty calldata. Plain ETH Transfer (NativeTransferPolicy) checks that."
  ],
  "solution": [
    {
      "fallback": "CALL",
      "policy": "CoSignerPolicy",
      "config": {
        "cosigner": "CoSigner"
      }
    },
    {
      "target": "MultiSend",
      "selector": "multiSend",
      "operation": "DELEGATECALL",
      "policy": "MultiSendPolicy"
    },
    {
      "target": "Safe",
      "selector": "addOwnerWithThreshold",
      "policy": "DenyPolicy"
    },
    {
      "target": "Dave",
      "selector": "none",
      "policy": "NativeTransferPolicy"
    }
  ],
  "explain": "Four rules, four jobs. The co-signer catch-all reviews anything new. The Batch Checker opens batches and sends each step back through the rules, so the co-signer signs steps, not the batch. Always Deny on adding owners wins over the catch-all, whoever co-signs. Plain ETH Transfer lets Dave receive ETH and nothing else. The DELEGATECALL catch-all stays empty, so unknown code never runs inside the Safe."
}
